t":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119245","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119245","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119245.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119245.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"Contributes to #43440\r\n\r\nAdds unit tests for `AStar2D` covering:\r\n\r\n* Pathfinding with an `ABCX` subclass overriding `_compute_cost`, mirroring the existing `AStar3D` tests\r\n* Adding/removing points and edges, including directed and bidirectional connections\r\n* Empty graph behavior (`get_point_count`, `has_point`, `get_point_ids`, path queries)\r\n* Point properties: position, weight scale, disabled state, and re-adding existing points\r\n* Capacity and ID helpers: `get_available_point_id`, `get_point_capacity`, `reserve_space`, `clear`\r\n* Geometry queries: `get_closest_point` and `get_closest_position_in_segment`\r\n* Path behavior with weight scales, disconnected graphs, partial paths, and disabled points\r\n* Invalid input handling for all public API `ERR_FAIL_COND` branches, wrapped with `ERR_PRINT_OFF` / `ERR_PRINT_ON` to keep test output clean\r\n\r\nAI disclosure: I used Claude Opus 4.7 to help draft the PR description and review my code before submission. I wrote the tests myself, but used it to polish wording and double-check coverage.\r\n","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119245/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119245/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}